      "customfield_10012" : "0|i0059r:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "TRACEROUTE",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Ø  Windows firewall (workaround/set to allow) and unix report error better for not root",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Ø  Variant of Traceroute/Ping that does callback – not gather into sequence – so more flexible.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Ø  Traceroute sampling support – maybe show min/max/median/mean instead of each sample.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Ø  WAG at (either do or document in BUG REPORT) – TCP/GRE/UDP support. There is a TCP/UDP echo service I think I can use. See sample traceroute code and see if that’s what it does.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Ø  IPv6 support",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Ø  Maybe do same separation of sampling in Traceroute we did for Ping? Maybe objectify Traceroute call? But at any rate – make it work with samples.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "---",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : ">>>> copy this code in Ping as starting point for traceroute and use it to do first draft impl of traceroute.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "              >> and do UDP-based ping/tracertoue and TCP, and GRE, etc – see traceroute.c sources. Maybe just open bug report to track this – do quicky icmp based one, and maybe leave rest for later",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
